/*! \page Materials_intro Material models (Layer 2)

\section Materials_intro_introduction Introduction

A material model is the host-specific half of RadCluster. It declares the populations of a host material, its admissible vertex and edge sets, and its rate kernels. It does not implement an integrator: the graph walker, the C++ solver, the preconditioner and the reductions of the \ref Core_intro are inherited unchanged.

| Layer | Location | Content |
|---|---|---|
| 1, abstract core | py_utils/core and cpp_utils/core | cluster identifier, edge classes, graph container, graph walker, state layout, reductions, CVODE driver |
| 2, material model | py_utils/materials and cpp_utils/materials | populations, admissible vertices and edges, rate kernels of one host |

\section Materials_intro_pages Pages

- \subpage Materials_eurofer97
- \subpage Materials_newHost

\sa \ref Core_intro

*/
